  "system": {
    "description": "<p>This medium-sized portable rocket extends struts, aims itself, and launches into a low polar orbit on any planet with gravity below 2 g. Over a 1-2 day period, it uses a variety of sensors (radar, visual, infrared, mass, spectrographic) to map the planet and beam this information back. The maps are low resolution, showing nothing less than 100 meters across, but it will identify large masses, cities, lights on the planet&rsquo;s dark side, atmospheric conditions, and data on the planet&rsquo;s rotation and gravity.</p>",
